  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "38137582",
      "title": "The Old @Effect Decorator & Registering Effects",
      "lectureOrder": 701,
      "videoOrder": 646,
      "sourceHash": "204528875774e933e1049c7e7192297c46a2f3ee4f00f91e2928a6053b6f32c3",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.16,
          "end": 3.96,
          "en": "Now, as a little extra note here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.96,
          "end": 5.04,
          "en": "I also wanna mention",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.04,
          "end": 9.6,
          "en": "that in the past when working with older versions of NgRx,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.6,
          "end": 13.14,
          "en": "the createEffect function here did not exist.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.14,
          "end": 15.96,
          "en": "And instead of registering an effect like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.96,
          "end": 19.86,
          "en": "you would've just registered this pipeline",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.86,
          "end": 22.41,
          "en": "as a value here in a property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.41,
          "end": 27.41,
          "en": "and you would've decorated it with the @Effect decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.66,
          "end": 31.74,
          "en": "And this decorator would've been imported from NgRx Effect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.74,
          "end": 36.74,
          "en": "but it's not supported in recent NgRx versions anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.99,
          "end": 38.97,
          "en": "In old versions, it was supported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.97,
          "end": 42.93,
          "en": "and you would've passed dispatch: false wrapped in an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.93,
          "end": 46.38,
          "en": "as a value to this @Effect decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 46.38,
          "end": 48.18,
          "en": "So this is how you would've written this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.18,
          "end": 51.42,
          "en": "in older versions, older NgRx versions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.42,
          "end": 53.85,
          "en": "In more recent versions as mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.85,
          "end": 56.61,
          "en": "the Effect decorator is not supported anymore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.61,
          "end": 60.45,
          "en": "and therefore, instead you wrap this pipeline",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.45,
          "end": 62.46,
          "en": "into a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.46,
          "end": 67.14,
          "en": "and pass that function to the createEffect function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.14,
          "end": 69.96000000000001,
          "en": "and you then simply pass this configuration object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.96000000000001,
          "end": 72.033,
          "en": "as a second value to createEffect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 73.32,
          "end": 76.28999999999999,
          "en": "So that's just something you should also be aware of.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.28999999999999,
          "end": 79.44,
          "en": "But with that, this effect is now registered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.44,
          "end": 84.15,
          "en": "And now to register it with NgRx, you should go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 84.15,
          "end": 88.02,
          "en": "to your main.ts file when using standalone components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 88.02,
          "end": 93.02000000000001,
          "en": "or the app module file when using modules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 93.36,
          "end": 97.02000000000001,
          "en": "And then there you have this provideEffects function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 97.02000000000001,
          "end": 99.577,
          "en": "or EffectsModule.forRoot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 100.95,
          "end": 104.78999999999999,
          "en": "And you would now simply pass an array to provideEffects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 104.78999999999999,
          "end": 108.42,
          "en": "or to EffectsModule.forRoot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 108.42,
          "end": 113.00999999999999,
          "en": "and pass your Effect classes that you have to this array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 113.00999999999999,
          "end": 117.50999999999999,
          "en": "So in this case, the CounterEffects class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 117.50999999999999,
          "end": 119.85,
          "en": "It is imported here and then passed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 119.85,
          "end": 122.853,
          "en": "as a value in this array to provideEffects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 124.35,
          "end": 127.56,
          "en": "And again, that's exactly the same if you're using modules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 127.56,
          "end": 132.06,
          "en": "So therefore here, I'll also copy the counter.effects file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 132.06,
          "end": 133.83,
          "en": "from my standalone component app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 133.83,
          "end": 137.253,
          "en": "into the store folder of the module-based app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 138.24,
          "end": 141.27,
          "en": "And then here I add CounterEffects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 142.638,
          "end": 144.54,
          "en": "to EffectsModule.forRoot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 144.54,
          "end": 146.853,
          "en": "And also add this import here, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 148.59,
          "end": 151.14,
          "en": "Now with that, there's just one additional thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 151.14,
          "end": 153.57,
          "en": "you should do in both applications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 153.57,
          "end": 156.81,
          "en": "This CounterEffects class should be decorated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 156.81,
          "end": 160.2,
          "en": "with the @Injectable decorator provided",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 160.2,
          "end": 161.76,
          "en": "by Angular to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 161.76,
          "end": 164.94,
          "en": "that it can successfully be injected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 164.94,
          "end": 168.06,
          "en": "So you should add this here to CounterEffects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 168.06,
          "end": 169.86,
          "en": "in the module-based application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 169.86,
          "end": 173.55,
          "en": "and also when using standalone components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 173.55,
          "end": 174.78,
          "en": "And of course, you must make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 174.78,
          "end": 177.993,
          "en": "that you also add the import from angular/core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 179.73,
          "end": 181.08,
          "en": "With that, however,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 181.08,
          "end": 183.72,
          "en": "you're able to serve this application no matter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 183.72,
          "end": 187.29,
          "en": "if you're using standalone components or modules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 187.29,
          "end": 189.36,
          "en": "And you can, therefore, then see your counters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 189.36,
          "end": 193.62,
          "en": "and decrement and increment them, and you will see that now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 193.62,
          "end": 195.87,
          "en": "if you open your console,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 195.87,
          "end": 200.87,
          "en": "the action object gets locked there because in my effect,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 201.48,
          "end": 204.72,
          "en": "I added this console.log line here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 204.72,
          "end": 208.35,
          "en": "And you will also see that if you go to application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 208.35,
          "end": 211.26,
          "en": "to your local storage, you got this count value here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 211.26,
          "end": 214.62,
          "en": "which is not the latest counter value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 214.62,
          "end": 217.11,
          "en": "but only the value by which it was changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 217.11,
          "end": 219.21,
          "en": "Something we will improve soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 219.21,
          "end": 221.523,
          "en": "But you see that this also works.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
